    "text": "Let me pull your bench history first. Let me check whether it's logged under a different name. I can't see any bench sessions logged, so I can't tell you where it stalled or by how much. If you've been training it outside the app, tell me your recent top sets and how long it's been stuck, and I can be specific.\n\nIn general, a stalled bench usually comes down to a few things:\n\n- **Volume:** Most people break through by adding a set or two of bench per week, or a second bench day, before adding any weight.\n- **Rep ranges:** Spend a few weeks in 6 to 8 reps with a load that leaves a rep or two in the tank, then work back toward heavier sets.\n- **Small jumps:** Add the smallest increments you can, and stop sets short of grinding every rep.\n- **Pressing muscles:** Triceps and shoulder work, like close-grip bench and overhead pressing, often move the bench when the bench itself won't.\n- **Recovery:** Sleep, eating enough, and a deload week if you've been grinding for a while.\n\nWant me to build a block with extra pressing volume, or tell me what your last few bench sessions looked like?",
